{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filename": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filepath": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "page": 7, "title": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "year": "2024", "row": 6}, "page_content": "\ufeffWhat is psoriasis and what are its common symptoms?: What are the common medications for treating acne?\nPsoriasis is a chronic autoimmune condition that results in the overproduction of skin cells. This overproduction leads to patches of thick, red skin covered with silvery scales. Common symptoms include red patches of skin covered with thick, silvery scales, small scaling spots (commonly seen in children), dry and cracked skin that may bleed, itching, burning, or soreness, thickened, pitted, or ridged nails, and swollen and stiff joints.: Acne treatments depend on the severity of the condition. Some common medications include:\r\n\r\n1. Retinoids and retinoid-like drugs: These come as creams, gels and lotions. Retinoid drugs are derived from vitamin A and include tretinoin, adapalene and tazarotene.\r\n\r\n2. Antibiotics: These may be applied to the skin or taken orally and work by reducing inflammation and bacteria.\r\n\r\n3. Salicylic acid and azelaic acid: These help prevent pores from becoming plugged.\r\n\r\n4. Dapsone: This is often used in combination with other medications and is especially effective for inflammatory acne.", "type": "Document"}}